<title>USA: US adj chain store sales off 1.7 pct - BTM/Schroders.</title>
<headline>US adj chain store sales off 1.7 pct - BTM/Schroders.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. chain store sales dropped 1.7 percent in the week ended September 7 from the prior week, according to the seasonally adjusted BTM/Schroders weekly chain store sales index.</p>
<p>Sales for the week were up 4.0 percent on a year-over-year basis, while the month-to-date index dropped 0.7 percent from the prior month.</p>
<p>&quot;Some retailers noted that Huricane Fran forced the closing of a few stores for about a day, but that impact was insignificant on the aggregate sales tally,&quot; a BTM Schroders report said. -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
